<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45355" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔτροχος</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		 and Lyr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰτρ</span>-, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, poet. metapl. acc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰτροχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>An. Ox.</u>
					1.271
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχός</span>):—<i>well-wheeled</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰτροχον ἅρμα καὶ ἵππους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.438
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				463
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμαξαν ἐΰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.150
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σατίναι ἐΰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				20a
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. κύκλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέχω</span>) <i>smoothlyrunning</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				37c
			</span></i>; <i>running easily</i>, of a cord put through loops, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				2.4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. γλῶσσα</span> a <i>ready,
				glib</i> tongue, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				268
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλῶσσα εὔ. ἐν τῷ διαλέγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Per.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			; of style, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				20
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τῆς φύσεως, τῆς διανοίας
			εὔ</span>., <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.240
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Isid.</u>
				80
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				32
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ σφαιροειδὲς ἡμῶν οὐκ
			εὔ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				2.2.2
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χως</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἀναγινώσκειν</span> to read
			<i>fluently</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.303
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>well-rounded, round</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεῖχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1389
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				 ii 13
			</span></i>.</div>
